WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.560
Friday, just before sunset.

2
00:00:02.610 --> 00:00:05.990
At least two candles are
lit, and a blessing is said.

3
00:00:06.040 --> 00:00:10.020
For about 25 hours there is
wine, two plaited loaves,

4
00:00:10.070 --> 00:00:12.880
songs and long family meals.

5
00:00:12.930 --> 00:00:17.030
It ends on Saturday night,
when three stars can be seen.

6
00:00:17.080 --> 00:00:21.850
So why would someone switch off
their phone for 25 hours every week,

7
00:00:21.900 --> 00:00:23.730
and call it a delight?

8
00:00:23.780 --> 00:00:28.000
In this mission, you'll follow Shabbat
from Friday sunset to Saturday night,

9
00:00:28.050 --> 00:00:30.260
at home and in the synagogue.

10
00:00:30.310 --> 00:00:34.780
Then you'll compare how Orthodox
and Reform Jews keep the day today.

11
00:00:34.830 --> 00:00:39.310
Your mission: find out why a weekly
day of rest is called a delight.
